casebook raw-consequent v1
source "regression fixture: a doubt that discards the consequent of an implies" dated 2026-10-14 by "quorum tests"
note "Reduced from a random rulebook on which tools/refcheck.py and cbc disagreed (2026-10-14)."
note "With r4, r5 and r7 all present: d4 discards r7, but the consistency doubt for 'implies r5 r7' reads r7 RAW, as"
note "documented, so r7 present means r5 is corroborated, c1 holds and the safe action a0 is chosen. cbc used to land"
note "d4's attack on the raw r7 itself, so the mismatch fired, r5 was discarded and idle_run was chosen; and writing"
note "'undermines r7' inside d4's declaration instead of on its own line gave the other answer."
observe r4 "reading r4"
observe r5 "reading r5"
observe r7 "reading r7"
claim c1 "c1" needs r5
claim c2 "c2" when any r7 r5
doubt d4 "d4" needs r5 r4
d4 undermines r7
implies r5 r7
r4 rebuts c2
action idle_run idle
action a0 safe when c1
action a1 when c2
prefer a0 over a1 over idle_run
